 - Instrumental Role of Warehouse Location
The warehouse location (Lat/Long) is the anchor for all Transit Management
.
Distance Calculation: It is essential to store these in Application Layer 2 to calculate travel duration (Departure Time + Expected Duration = Destination ETA)
.
Slot Selection: Without the warehouse coordinate, the system cannot use the Geoapify Routing API to provide the route-based ETA that proves if a driver's rebooking request is physically possible
.
Reverse-Trip Priority: By tracking the Current Physical Warehouse of drivers/trucks relative to their Assigned/Home Warehouse, you can use location data to prioritize shipments that get resources back to their base, reducing empty miles
.
