Web UI Dashboard Implementation (Destination Warehouse Focus)
The dashboard must be modular, representing one card or section per warehouse (A-F) to manage the specific operational view of each site
.
Warehouse Operational Section (Repeated for A, B, C, D, E, F)
Resource Summary: Real-time counters for available Drivers, Trucks, Staff, and Machinery currently physically present at that location
.
Slot Timeline: A visual calendar showing Gate-level occupancy (e.g., Gates A1-A6) with color-coded status: Confirmed, Pending, or In-Progress
.
Yard Snapshot: A live feed of trucks currently "Arrived" (in yard), "Docked" (unloading), or "Upcoming" (expected based on ETA)
.
Integrated Escalation & Admin Control
The dashboard correlates each warehouse view with an Escalation Panel. As an FDE Architect, the following logic must be executed:
Contextual Routing: Escalations are automatically tagged by Warehouse ID and Urgency (LOW to CRITICAL)
.
Actionable Tickets: Every escalation must display the Shipment ID, Reason (e.g., "No slots available within 3 hours"), and a Thread Link to the driver conversation
.
Manual Overrides: The Admin uses this section to handle "out-of-scope" decisions such as commercial penalty approvals or overriding physical safety constraints that the AI is prohibited from deciding
.
Auditability: Every resolution in this section generates a SHIPMENT_RESOLVED event, capturing the actor ID and previous state for historical traceability